"""Bundled DSA concept notes — the shared knowledge base the mentor teaches from (RAG corpus)."""

KNOWLEDGE = [
    {"topic": "arrays-and-hashing", "content": "Arrays & Hashing: Use a hash map (dict/set) to trade memory for speed, turning O(n^2) lookups into O(1) average. Core patterns: frequency counting, seen-set membership, index mapping, prefix counts. Classic problems: Two Sum, Group Anagrams, Top K Frequent Elements, Longest Consecutive Sequence, Contains Duplicate. Ask yourself: can a dict remember what I have already seen?"},
    {"topic": "two-pointers", "content": "Two Pointers: Two indices that move through the array based on a condition — converging (sorted pair sum), fast/slow (cycle detection), or parallel arrays. Works best on sorted data or linked structures. Classic problems: Two Sum II, 3Sum, Container With Most Water, Trapping Rain Water, Valid Palindrome, Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array."},
    {"topic": "sliding-window", "content": "Sliding Window: Maintain a contiguous window [left..right] and update counts incrementally instead of recomputing. Fixed size for 'max average of k elements', variable size for 'longest substring without repeating characters' or 'at most K distinct'. Classic problems: Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters, Minimum Window Substring, Longest Repeating Character Replacement, Max Consecutive Ones III, Permutation in String."},
    {"topic": "stack", "content": "Stack: LIFO for nested structures and 'nearest greater/smaller element' problems. Monotonic stack keeps elements sorted to answer next-greater queries in O(n). Classic problems: Valid Parentheses, Min Stack, Daily Temperatures, Largest Rectangle in Histogram, Next Greater Element I/II, Decode String."},
    {"topic": "binary-search", "content": "Binary Search: Halve the search space each step on monotonic data — sorted arrays, answer ranges, or predicate boundaries. Watch off-by-one: use while left < right with a well-defined mid decision. Classic problems: Standard Binary Search, Search in Rotated Sorted Array, Find Minimum in Rotated Sorted Array, Koko Eating Bananas, Median of Two Sorted Arrays, Time Based Key-Value Store."},
    {"topic": "linked-list", "content": "Linked List: Fast/slow pointers find middles and detect cycles; dummy head simplifies edge cases; reversal is a core interview skill (iterative prev/curr swap). Classic problems: Reverse Linked List, Merge Two Sorted Lists, Linked List Cycle, Reorder List, Remove Nth Node From End, LRU Cache (with hashmap + doubly linked list), Merge K Sorted Lists (with heap)."},
    {"topic": "trees", "content": "Trees: DFS (preorder/inorder/postorder) with recursion; BFS (level order) with a queue. Many tree problems reduce to 'do something at each node while returning info upward' (height, depth, diameter, balance). Classic problems: Invert Binary Tree, Maximum Depth, Same Tree, Subtree of Another Tree, Lowest Common Ancestor, Binary Tree Level Order Traversal, Validate BST, Binary Tree Right Side View, Diameter of Binary Tree."},
    {"topic": "binary-search-tree", "content": "BST: Inorder traversal yields sorted order. Search/insert/delete are O(h). Property: left subtree < node < right subtree — validate with min/max bounds, not just neighbor comparison. Classic problems: Validate BST, Kth Smallest Element in a BST, LCA of BST, Insert into BST, Convert Sorted Array to BST, BST Iterator."},
    {"topic": "heap-priority-queue", "content": "Heap / Priority Queue: O(log n) push/pop of min or max. Use for 'top k', streaming medians, merged streams, and greedy scheduling. Python: heapq (min-heap; negate values for max-heap). Classic problems: Kth Largest Element in a Stream, Last Stone Weight, K Closest Points to Origin, Kth Largest Element in an Array, Task Scheduler, Find Median from Data Stream (two heaps)."},
    {"topic": "backtracking", "content": "Backtracking: Build candidates incrementally, abandon a branch as soon as it violates constraints, and undo the choice. Think choose → explore → un-choose. Classic problems: Subsets, Combination Sum, Permutations, Subsets II, Word Search, Palindrome Partitioning, N-Queens, Letter Combinations of a Phone Number."},
    {"topic": "tries", "content": "Trie (Prefix Tree): Store strings character by character for O(L) insert/search/prefix queries. Node children in a dict; mark end-of-word. Classic problems: Implement Trie, Design Add and Search Words (with wildcards), Word Search II, Longest Common Prefix of strings."},
    {"topic": "graphs-bfs", "content": "Graph BFS: Level-by-level traversal with a queue — gives shortest path in unweighted graphs and is the tool for flood fill and nearest-source problems (multi-source BFS by seeding the queue with all sources). Classic problems: Number of Islands, Rotting Oranges, 01 Matrix, Word Ladder, Shortest Path in Binary Matrix, Clone Graph."},
    {"topic": "graphs-dfs", "content": "Graph DFS: Recursive or stack-based exploration to visit all reachable nodes, count components, or detect cycles. Track visited to avoid infinite loops. Classic problems: Number of Islands, Max Area of Island, Pacific Atlantic Water Flow, Course Schedule (cycle detect), Surrounded Regions, Number of Connected Components."},
    {"topic": "topological-sort", "content": "Topological Sort: Linear order of a DAG where every edge goes forward. Kahn's algorithm (BFS with in-degrees) or DFS + reverse finish order. If the sort covers fewer than all nodes, a cycle exists. Classic problems: Course Schedule I/II, Alien Dictionary, Minimum Height Trees, Parallel Courses."},
    {"topic": "union-find", "content": "Union-Find (Disjoint Set): Tracks connected components under union operations with near-O(1) amortized cost using path compression + union by rank. Classic problems: Number of Provinces, Redundant Connection, Accounts Merge, Most Stones Removed, Satisfiability of Equality Equations."},
    {"topic": "shortest-path", "content": "Shortest Path: Dijkstra for non-negative weights (heap + dist map), Bellman-Ford for possible negative edges (V-1 relaxation rounds), BFS for unweighted, 0-1 BFS with deque for 0/1 weights. Classic problems: Network Delay Time, Cheapest Flights Within K Stops (Bellman-Ford variant), Path With Minimum Effort, Swim in Rising Water."},
    {"topic": "dynamic-programming", "content": "Dynamic Programming intro: Overlapping subproblems + optimal substructure. Steps: 1) define the state clearly, 2) write the recurrence, 3) identify base cases, 4) implement top-down (memo) or bottom-up (table), 5) optimize space if possible. Classic problems: Climbing Stairs, House Robber I/II, Coin Change, Word Break, Unique Paths."},
    {"topic": "1d-dp", "content": "1D DP: dp[i] answers the question for prefix ending at i, built from a few earlier entries. Classic problems: Climbing Stairs (dp[i]=dp[i-1]+dp[i-2]), House Robber (skip or take), Coin Change (min coins for amount), Longest Increasing Subsequence (O(n^2) or patience sorting O(n log n)), Word Break, Maximum Subarray (Kadane's)."},
    {"topic": "2d-dp", "content": "2D DP: dp[i][j] over two indices — grids or two-sequence comparison. Common recurrences: path counts (sum from top/left) and edit distance style (match/mismatch choice). Classic problems: Unique Paths, Minimum Path Sum, Longest Common Subsequence, Edit Distance, Distinct Subsequences, Interleaving String, Longest Palindromic Substring."},
    {"topic": "knapsack", "content": "Knapsack family: 0/1 (each item once — iterate capacity backwards), unbounded (items reusable — iterate forwards), and subset-sum variants (target reachable?). Classic problems: Partition Equal Subset Sum, Target Sum, Coin Change I/II, Last Stone Weight II, Ones and Zeroes."},
    {"topic": "greedy", "content": "Greedy: Make the locally best choice and prove it never hurts. Usually needs sorting by some key first (end time, start time, ratio). Classic problems: Maximum Subarray, Jump Game I/II, Gas Station, Hand of Straights, Merge Triplets to Form Target, Partition Labels, Activity/Meeting Rooms scheduling."},
    {"topic": "intervals", "content": "Intervals: Sort by start (or end) then sweep, merging overlaps or tracking free rooms with a heap. Classic problems: Insert Interval, Merge Intervals, Non-overlapping Intervals, Meeting Rooms I/II, Minimum Interval to Include Each Query."},
    {"topic": "math-and-number-theory", "content": "Math & Number Theory: GCD (Euclid), primes (Sieve of Eratosthenes), modular arithmetic, fast power, digit manipulation. Watch overflow in other languages; in Python use divmod and pow(a, b, m). Classic problems: Rotate Image, Spiral Matrix, Set Matrix Zeroes, Happy Number, Pow(x, n), Count Primes, Excel Sheet Column Title."},
    {"topic": "bit-manipulation", "content": "Bit Manipulation: XOR cancels pairs (a^a=0), n & (n-1) clears lowest set bit, shifts emulate multiply/divide by 2. Classic problems: Single Number, Number of 1 Bits, Counting Bits, Reverse Bits, Missing Number, Sum of Two Integers, Reverse Integer."},
    {"topic": "prefix-sum", "content": "Prefix Sum: pre[i] = sum of first i elements lets any range sum be answered in O(1) as pre[j] - pre[i-1]. 2D variant answers rectangle sums. Combined with hashmap: count subarrays with sum K. Classic problems: Range Sum Query Immutable, Subarray Sum Equals K, Product of Array Except Self, Continuous Subarray Sum, Find Pivot Index."},
    {"topic": "matrix-traversal", "content": "Matrix Traversal: Treat as a graph — BFS/DFS flood fill from cells; in-place tricks: first row/col as markers (Set Matrix Zeroes), rotate via transpose + reverse. Classic problems: Number of Islands, Flood Fill, Rotate Image, Spiral Matrix, Set Matrix Zeroes, Word Search."},
]
